From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:15:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: let an i386 FlushInstructionCache reach the
 emulator

Wine's i386 and x86-64 kernelbase return TRUE from FlushInstructionCache
without a syscall: x86 caches are coherent. Here an i386 process runs
under WoW64 on an ARM64 host, as on Windows on ARM, and FEX learns of
code rewritten in place from wow64's NtFlushInstructionCache
(BTCpuFlushInstructionCache2) or from its write-protect trap. The trap
misses a 4 KiB page that shares a 16 KiB host page with writable pages:
the host page stays writable. The childabort probe (i386) rewrites
`mov eax, imm32; ret` in such a page and flushes; 87.5 % of its calls
returned the value written before, all but the first call on each page.

The i386 FlushInstructionCache now calls NtFlushInstructionCache, as
Windows' does. The x86-64 one is not built here and is unchanged.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-12-jit-alias-release.md
Offered-upstream: no; WoW64 on an ARM64 Linux host has the same no-op and could take it
---
 dlls/kernelbase/memory.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/memory.c b/dlls/kernelbase/memory.c
index 97e6bf5..e6eec6d 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/memory.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/memory.c
@@ -132,7 +132,17 @@ BOOL WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH FlushViewOfFile( const void *base, SIZE_T size )
 /****************************************************************************
  *           FlushInstructionCache   (kernelbase.@)
  */
-#if defined(__i386__) || defined(__x86_64__)
+#ifdef __i386__
+/* An i386 process here runs under WoW64 on an ARM64 host, as on Windows on
+ * ARM: the flush must reach wow64's NtFlushInstructionCache, which tells the
+ * emulator (BTCpuFlushInstructionCache2) to translate the range again. The
+ * emulator's write-protect detection of changed code misses a 4 KiB page that
+ * shares a 16 KiB host page with writable pages. */
+BOOL WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH FlushInstructionCache( HANDLE process, LPCVOID addr, SIZE_T size )
+{
+    return set_ntstatus( NtFlushInstructionCache( process, addr, size ));
+}
+#elif defined(__x86_64__)
 BOOL WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH FlushInstructionCache( HANDLE process, LPCVOID addr, SIZE_T size )
 {
     /* X86 processors have coherent instruction and data caches, no need to do anything */
